      en: ["Silves Castle covers an area of roughly 1.2 hectares and features 11 towers.", "The town was the capital of the Algarve region under Moorish rule until 1242.", "The underground cisterns are still used today to host cultural exhibitions.", "Silves Cathedral is considered the most important Gothic monument in the Algarve.", "King Sancho I initially took the city in 1189, though it was later lost and retaken.", "The Roman bridge in Silves was actually rebuilt in the 15th century on older foundations."],
